    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d442">

                <pb facs="0617" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg521"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.1216M/502</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-12-05"><hi rendition="#italic">December 5,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received December 20.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4648</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s No. 1860
                    of November 23, 1921,<anchor n="43" xml:id="d442-f1"/> I have the honor to
                    report that <hi rendition="#italic">El Universal</hi> of the third instant
                    published an article to the effect that cotton-growers of Arizona and California
                    are seeking by means of dams and impoundings altogether to deprive Mexicans of
                    the waters of the Colorado River to which they are justly entitled pursuant to
                    the Guadalupe Treaty signed in 1848.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d442-f2"/> The
                    article added that the Department of Communications and Public Works had
                    appointed Mr. Manuel Balarezo, Civil Engineer, to represent Mexico’s interests
                    at the conferences presently to be held in San Francisco, California.</p>
                <pb facs="0618" n="522" xml:id="pg522"/>
                <p>The local press of the fourth instant stated that the following committee has
                    been appointed by General Obregón to attend the conference which is to be held
                    at Riverside, California, and at which will be discussed the utilization of the
                    waters of the Colorado River: <list>
                        <item>President, Engineer Federico Ramos,</item>
                        <item>Engineer Manuel Balarezo,</item>
                        <item>Engineer Javier Sánchez Mejorada.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>It is stated further that the appointment of the commission has been communicated
                    to the Secretary-Treasury of the League of the Southwest, in response to its
                    telegram dated December second, in which the League announced its desire to
                    accord due honors and hospitality to the Mexican Commission and requested
                    information as to the number and names of its members, date of arrival, etc.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George T.
                    Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
